!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = crispr library: whole-genome Brunello
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = valine concentration: high - 20V
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = time point: 4 days post passage into differential valine media
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = molecule subtype: CRISPR sgRNA
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = For the whole genome screen, the infected cells were cultured in standard or low valine media.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA was isolated using Qiagen DNA purfication kit for tRNA screen and Takara Nucleospin Blood XL kit.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries were prepared by amplification of the sgRNA with primers compatible for Illumina sequencing.
!Sample_description = CUTLL1_CRISPR_Brunello_normalized-results.tsv
!Sample_description = CUTLL1_CRISPR_Brunello_CERES-scores.tsv
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: CRISPR sgRNA screen
!Sample_data_processing = Trimming: Adapter sequences were first trimmed off using cutadapt, removing all untrimmed reads (parameters -e 0.1 -O 10 -m 20 –discard-untrimmed)
!Sample_data_processing = Counting: Trimmed 20bp reads were counted by exact matches with the sgRNA library sequences.
!Sample_data_processing = Normalization: Raw reads were intra-sample normalized with edgeR function cpm.
!Sample_data_processing = Differential analysis: First, log2 fold-changes based on CPM values between different valine conditions and repsective treatment days were calculated with a pseudocount of 0.1.
!Sample_data_processing = Gene summary: To summarize individual sgRNAs on a gene-level, we executed the R-package "ceres" to report essentiality scores per gene, using log2 fold-changes..
